s and nothing happened in either heat or semi-final to discourage the opinion that the American would be Olympic champion. Peirsol trailed early leader " [:a {:href "/athletes/93284"} "Matt Welsh"] " at the halfway point then took the race apart on the final length, winning comfortably ahead  of " [:a {:href "/athletes/93288"} "Markus Rogan"] " of Austria with Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/103417"} "Tomomi Morita"] " touching ahead of defending champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/93856"} "Lenny Krayzelburg"] ", by a mere two hundredths of a second.\nPeirsol’s victory was the 12th win by an American in this event but, in contrast, Rogan’s medal the first by Austrian for 92 years. Piersol would return in 2008 to become the first man to successfully defend his Olympic title since " [:a {:href "/athletes/47595"} "Roland Matthes"] " in 1972."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93859"} "Aaron Peirsol"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "54.65 (2 h6)"] [:td {} "54.34 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "54.06 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93288"} "Markus Rogan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} "54.87 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "54.42 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "54.35 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103417"} "Tomomi Morita"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {: